The graph of $y=ax^2+bx+c$ is given below, where $a$, $b$, and $c$ are integers.  Find $a-b+c$.

[asy]
size(150);

Label f;

f.p=fontsize(4);

xaxis(-3,3,Ticks(f, 1.0));

yaxis(-4,4,Ticks(f, 1.0));

real f(real x)

{

return x^2+2x-1;

}

draw(graph(f,-2.7,.7),linewidth(1),Arrows(6));
[/asy]

For some constants $a$ and $b,$ let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
ax + b & \text{if } x < 2, \\
8 - 3x & \text{if } x \ge 2.
\end{array}
\right.\]The function $f$ has the property that $f(f(x)) = x$ for all $x.$ What is $a + b?$

